      "claim": "The captured militia member does not qualify as a prisoner of war under Article 4A(2) because he fails the requirement of a fixed distinctive sign recognizable at a distance.",
      "reasoning": "Article 4(2) of the Third Geneva Convention lists the conditions that other militias must satisfy to be entitled to POW status. While the militia satisfies the command, open‑carrying, and law‑compliance conditions, it deliberately wears ordinary civilian clothing without any insignia, thereby lacking the \"fixed distinctive sign recognizable at a distance\" required by paragraph (b). Consequently, the militia member falls outside the category of persons entitled to POW status.",
