          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "gc_iii",
          "article": "art.4",
          "quoted_text": "(b) that of having a fixed distinctive sign recognizable at a distance;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Even if the militia member fails the distinctive‑sign requirement, Protocol I creates a presumption of POW status that must be respected until a competent tribunal determines otherwise.",
      "reasoning": "Article 45 of Additional Protocol I provides that any person who takes part in hostilities and falls into the power of an adverse Party is presumed to be a prisoner of war and shall continue to enjoy that status \"until such time as his status has been determined by a competent tribunal\" when doubt arises. The captured individual is a combatant who has fallen into Ardovian hands, and Ardovia has expressed doubt about his status. Therefore, under the presumption, he must be treated as a POW pending a formal determination.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "ap_i",
          "article": "art.45",
          "quoted_text": "A person who takes part in hostilities and falls into the power of an adverse Party shall be presumed to be a prisoner of war, and therefore shall be protected by the Third Convention, if he claims the status of prisoner of war, or if he appears to be entitled to such status, or if the Party on which he depends claims such status on his behalf by notification to the detaining Power or to the Protecting Power. Should any doubt arise as to whether any such person is entitled to the status of prisoner of war, he shall continue to have such status and, therefore, to be protected by the Third Convention and this Protocol until such time as his status has been determined by a competent tribunal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Ardovia is obligated to afford the captured militia member POW protections at least temporarily and to refer the status question to a competent tribunal in accordance with Protocol I.",
      "reasoning": "The presumption in Article 45 creates a procedural duty: when doubt exists, the detaining power must not deprive the individual of POW protections and must allow the status to be adjudicated by a competent tribunal. This duty overrides any immediate classification based solely on the distinctive‑sign deficiency. Accordingly, Ardovia must treat the individual as a POW until a tribunal decides whether the lack of a distinctive sign removes him from the category.",
      "citations": [
